    "updated_at": "2018-08-13T14:02:29Z",
    "body": "For clarifing the concept of an additional level of independent text content to average readers who are not familar with bidi knowledge, I suggest the spec also provide an example for the `<div>`, like the following one(Although it's recommened to do so with qutation marks or at least with `<span>`, it serves as an example of the concept of an additional level of independent text content, and illustrates how `div`s can change content semantics. RIght now I cannot come up with a better example):\r\n\r\n```\r\n<div><div>His reply is short</div> is short.</div>\r\n<div>His reply is <div>short is short</div>.</div>\r\n```",
    "author_association": "NONE",
