    "created_at": "2018-08-13T17:16:20Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-08-13T17:24:00Z",
    "body": "In general there is a distinction between semantic meaning and bidirectional isolation, so I believe this is still accurate. For example, your use of div as a replacement for `<q>` is not semantically correct.\r\n\r\nRemember that \"has no special meaning\" is different from \"has no effect at all\". Using `<div>` has many effects, e.g. on styling and CSS box generation, as well as bidirectional isolation. That doesn't change the fact that, unlike `<q>` or `<strong>` or other elements, using `<div>` conveys no semantic meaning from the author to the consumer.\r\n\r\nI'm not an expert in this area, but I'm hopeful our i18n experts can weigh in and clear up any confusion. Tagging as such.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
