    "updated_at": "2018-08-13T19:09:40Z",
    "body": "I'll try to repeat that the UA stylesheet in particular, and CSS styling in general, _is unrelated to semantics_. div can default to `display: block` and still have no semantic meaning. It can also default to `unicode-bidi: isolate` and have no semantic meaning. A page author can even make it `background: red`, and that doesn't change the fact that it has no semantic meaning. Styling and semantics are separate.\r\n\r\nAs for why divs are bidi-isolated, it appears that's part of a larger effort to ensure that elements which are by default display: block also by default bidi-isolated. So your question also applies to address, blockquote, center, div, figure, ...",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
