    "updated_at": "2018-08-13T19:23:01Z",
    "body": "Sorry for my poor English, maybe you got me wrong because I wasn't clear.\r\n\r\nYes, of course semantics and styling are separate domains, I knew it, but that was not I was trying to talk about.\r\n\r\nI was just talking about `unicode-bidi: isolate`'s being undesirable as a default for an element that conveys no meaning, so I just suggested to change `div` to add semantics on text context isolation, so it caters to default CSS.\r\n\r\nYou just said `unicode-bidi: isolate` is intended to be used for `display: block`. But `unicode-bidi` only takes effect on inline elements, and it's not inheritable, so I believe it is exclusively used for inline divs.",
