    "created_at": "2018-08-13T21:19:16Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-08-13T21:19:16Z",
    "body": "My understanding is that \"being an independent bidi\" is specified in CSS for those elements, including for div. Thus, that is *styling*, and *not a semantic feature of the elements*.\r\n\r\nAt this point I don't think futher discussion from me will be fruitful; I've already stated as clearly as I can my understanding that these are separate things and that div's \"has no semantics\" is not impacted by its default styles. (I.e., that it would be *incorrect* to update the spec's statement on an element's semantics due to that element's default styles, because that would be *making styling affect semantics*.) Maybe others, perhaps including i18n experts, will be able to explain the situation better.",
