    "body": "Thanks. So, your answer confirmed the spec won't cater to reality default css, and just left unicode-bidi isolation for inline divs to render in a default way that by default doesn't follow document semantics.\r\n\r\nI think your answer is somewhat reasonable, and I kinda understand your unwillingness for changing html standards to specially catering to default css.\r\n\r\nOf course it makes more sense to let ua css cater to html, not the other way around. It's just unfortunate that the wrong default css value has already been applied to the real world for a long time, so it's even harder for default css to cater to html, or they would break web.",
