    "created_at": "2018-08-15T15:08:13Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-08-15T15:15:23Z",
    "body": "Thankfully. My words didn't carry much weight. What @r12a , an expert, said might carry weight, and now I think people can now be convinced that bidi hehaviour can NEVER be left as pure presentation, it ALWAYS changes the meaning of the text content to the readers.\r\n\r\nBecause he said they strongly discourage people from directly setting `unicode-bidi` values, instead, they recommend use of HTML markups(`<bdo>`, `<bdi>`). That is the evident.\r\n\r\nAs to the second point @r12a made, I'd like to try to reword it, based on my understanding: the second point he made seemd to be suggesting that `div`'s defaulting to `unicode-bidi: isolate` is due to the historic reasons(back to the pre-HTML5 era, when: 1. there were no markups such as `article`, `section` etc., 2. `div`s were used \"semantically\", 3. \"isolate\" was just the \"built-in default\" behaviour in UAs for those markups before the actual `unicode-bidi` property was introduced). So the default CSS wanted to keep the compatibility due to those historic reasons. Is my rewording correct?",
